IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er3-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), regulations 52 and 53: LOSS OF PART-TIME EMPLOYMENT DUE TO
-- WORK STOPPAGE, and TERMINATION OF WORK STOPPAGE.
-- Written by the piece agent er3 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24 from the unofficial plain-text rendering
-- SOR-96-332.txt; nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- Out of range: s 36 of the Act (disentitlement for a stoppage of work caused by a labour dispute, piece ei2),
-- including the events of its paragraphs (a) and (b) that end it, and s 14 of the Act (the weekly insurable
-- earnings, piece ei1). Each is an input.

§ `Regulation 52 -- loss of part-time employment due to a work stoppage`

-- (2) The days of disentitlement in a week follow the percentage that is "the ratio between the claimant's average
-- weekly insurable earnings in that part-time employment and the weekly insurable earnings as determined under
-- section 14 of the Act", by the table: column I (percentage) to column II (days). The bands are "more than X but
-- not more than Y": the upper end belongs to the band. A ratio of nothing, or less, is below the table: NOTHING.
-- src:788 | (2) Where a claimant loses a part-time employment or is unable to resume a part-time employment for any reason mentioned in subsection 36(1) of the Act, the number of days of disentitlement of the claimant in a week is, for the percentage that is set out in column I of the table to this subsection and that is the ratio between the claimant’s average weekly insurable earnings in that part-time employment and the weekly insurable earnings as determined under section 14 of the Act, the corresponding number of days of disentitlement set out in column II of that table, ending on the occurrence, in respect of the part-time employment, of an event referred to in paragraph 36(1)(a) or (b) of the Act.
-- src:790 | Column I | Column II
-- src:791 | Percentage | Number of Days of Disentitlement
-- src:792 | more than 0 but not more than 10 | 0
-- src:793 | more than 10 but not more than 30 | 1
-- src:794 | more than 30 but not more than 50 | 2
-- src:795 | more than 50 but not more than 70 | 3
-- src:796 | more than 70 but not more than 90 | 4
-- src:797 | more than 90 | 5
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 52(2) (src:788) (src:790-797)
GIVEN `the claimant's average weekly insurable earnings in that part-time employment` IS A NUMBER
      `the weekly insurable earnings as determined under section 14 of the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 52(2) the days of disentitlement in a week according to the table` IS
    IF `the weekly insurable earnings as determined under section 14 of the Act` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE
        BRANCH
            --         column I: the ratio as a percentage            column II: days
            IF `the claimant's average weekly insurable earnings in that part-time employment` AT MOST 0                                                          THEN NOTHING
            IF `the claimant's average weekly insurable earnings in that part-time employment` AT MOST (10% TIMES `the weekly insurable earnings as determined under section 14 of the Act`) THEN JUST 0   -- more than 0 but not more than 10
            IF `the claimant's average weekly insurable earnings in that part-time employment` AT MOST (30% TIMES `the weekly insurable earnings as determined under section 14 of the Act`) THEN JUST 1   -- more than 10 but not more than 30
            IF `the claimant's average weekly insurable earnings in that part-time employment` AT MOST (50% TIMES `the weekly insurable earnings as determined under section 14 of the Act`) THEN JUST 2   -- more than 30 but not more than 50
            IF `the claimant's average weekly insurable earnings in that part-time employment` AT MOST (70% TIMES `the weekly insurable earnings as determined under section 14 of the Act`) THEN JUST 3   -- more than 50 but not more than 70
            IF `the claimant's average weekly insurable earnings in that part-time employment` AT MOST (90% TIMES `the weekly insurable earnings as determined under section 14 of the Act`) THEN JUST 4   -- more than 70 but not more than 90
            OTHERWISE JUST 5                                                                                                                                       -- more than 90

-- (1) "Subject to subsection (2)", the maximum is five days of disentitlement per week, "ending on the occurrence,
-- in respect of the part-time employment, of an event referred to in paragraph 36(1)(a) or (b) of the Act". Once
-- such an event has occurred there is no further disentitlement. The days for a week are the table's (2), and
-- never more than five.
-- src:787 | 52 (1) Subject to subsection (2), where a claimant loses a part-time employment or is unable to resume a part-time employment for any reason mentioned in subsection 36(1) of the Act, the maximum number of days of disentitlement of the claimant is five days per week ending on the occurrence, in respect of the part-time employment, of an event referred to in paragraph 36(1)(a) or (b) of the Act.
-- src:788 | (2) Where a claimant loses a part-time employment or is unable to resume a part-time employment for any reason mentioned in subsection 36(1) of the Act, the number of days of disentitlement of the claimant in a week is, for the percentage that is set out in column I of the table to this subsection and that is the ratio between the claimant’s average weekly insurable earnings in that part-time employment and the weekly insurable earnings as determined under section 14 of the Act, the corresponding number of days of disentitlement set out in column II of that table, ending on the occurrence, in respect of the part-time employment, of an event referred to in paragraph 36(1)(a) or (b) of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 52(1), (2) (src:787-788)
GIVEN `the claimant loses a part-time employment or is unable to resume a part-time employment for a reason mentioned in subsection 36(1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an event referred to in paragraph 36(1)(a) or (b) of the Act has occurred in respect of the part-time employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's average weekly insurable earnings in that part-time employment` IS A NUMBER
      `the weekly insurable earnings as determined under section 14 of the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 52 the days of disentitlement for the week` IS
    IF NOT (`the claimant loses a part-time employment or is unable to resume a part-time employment for a reason mentioned in subsection 36(1) of the Act`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `an event referred to in paragraph 36(1)(a) or (b) of the Act has occurred in respect of the part-time employment`
         THEN JUST 0
         ELSE CONSIDER `reg 52(2) the days of disentitlement in a week according to the table` `the claimant's average weekly insurable earnings in that part-time employment` `the weekly insurable earnings as determined under section 14 of the Act`
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
              WHEN JUST days THEN JUST (min 5 days)

§ `Regulation 53 -- termination of a work stoppage`

-- What occurrence, if any, prevents the attainment of at least 85 per cent of the normal level of the work-force or
-- of the activity (subsection (2)).
-- src:803 | (2) Where, in respect of a stoppage of work, an occurrence prevents the attainment of at least 85 per cent of the normal level of the work-force or activity in respect of the production of goods or services at a factory, workshop or other premises, the stoppage of work terminates
-- src:804 | (a) if the occurrence is a discontinuance of business, a permanent restructuring of activity or an act of God, when the level of the work-force or of the activity attains at least 85 per cent of that normal level, with the normal level adjusted by taking that occurrence into account; and
-- src:805 | (b) if the occurrence is a change in economic or market conditions or in technology, when
-- src:806 | (i) there is a resumption of activity at the factory, workshop or other premises, and
-- src:807 | (ii) the level of the work-force and of the activity attains at least 85 per cent of that normal level as adjusted by taking that occurrence into account.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 53(2) (src:803-807)
DECLARE `er3 Occurrence preventing the attainment of the 85 per cent level` IS ONE OF
    `er3 occurrence: none`
    `er3 occurrence: a discontinuance of business`                           -- (2)(a)
    `er3 occurrence: a permanent restructuring of activity`                  -- (2)(a)
    `er3 occurrence: an act of God`                                          -- (2)(a)
    `er3 occurrence: a change in economic or market conditions`              -- (2)(b)
    `er3 occurrence: a change in technology`                                 -- (2)(b)

-- (3) For the percentages of (1) and (2) "no account shall be taken of exceptional or temporary measures taken by
-- the employer before and during the stoppage of work for the purpose of offsetting the effects of the stoppage":
-- the part of a level that is due to such measures is left out of it.
-- src:808 | (3) For the purposes of calculating the percentages referred to in subsections (1) and (2), no account shall be taken of exceptional or temporary measures taken by the employer before and during the stoppage of work for the purpose of offsetting the effects of the stoppage.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 53(3) (src:808)
GIVEN `the level reached` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of that level due to exceptional or temporary measures taken by the employer to offset the effects of the stoppage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 53(3) the level to be counted` IS
    `the level reached` MINUS `the part of that level due to exceptional or temporary measures taken by the employer to offset the effects of the stoppage`

-- At least 85 per cent of a normal level: the level counted is at least 85 per cent of the normal level.
-- A normal level that is nothing or less cannot be measured against: NOTHING.
-- src:800 | 53 (1) For the purposes of section 36 of the Act and subject to subsection (2), a stoppage of work at a factory, workshop or other premises is terminated when
-- src:801 | (a) the work-force at the factory, workshop or other premises attains at least 85 per cent of its normal level; and
-- src:802 | (b) the level of activity in respect of the production of goods or services at the factory, workshop or other premises attains at least 85 per cent of its normal level.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 53(1) (src:800-802)
GIVEN `the level reached` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of that level due to exceptional or temporary measures taken by the employer to offset the effects of the stoppage` IS A NUMBER
      `the normal level` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 53 the level to be counted is at least 85 per cent of the normal level` IS
    IF `the normal level` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST ((`reg 53(3) the level to be counted` `the level reached` `the part of that level due to exceptional or temporary measures taken by the employer to offset the effects of the stoppage`) AT LEAST (85% TIMES `the normal level`))

-- (1) A stoppage of work at a factory, workshop or other premises is terminated when (a) the work-force and (b)
-- the level of activity in the production of goods or services have each reached at least 85 per cent of their
-- normal level. This is the case where no occurrence under (2) prevents it.
-- src:800 | 53 (1) For the purposes of section 36 of the Act and subject to subsection (2), a stoppage of work at a factory, workshop or other premises is terminated when
-- src:801 | (a) the work-force at the factory, workshop or other premises attains at least 85 per cent of its normal level; and
-- src:802 | (b) the level of activity in respect of the production of goods or services at the factory, workshop or other premises attains at least 85 per cent of its normal level.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 53(1) (src:800-802)
GIVEN `the work-force at the premises is at least 85 per cent of its normal level` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the level of activity at the premises is at least 85 per cent of its normal level` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 53(1) the stoppage of work is terminated` IS
    CONSIDER `the work-force at the premises is at least 85 per cent of its normal level`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `the level of activity at the premises is at least 85 per cent of its normal level`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST activity THEN (IF activity THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE)
    WHEN JUST workforce THEN
        IF workforce
        THEN `the level of activity at the premises is at least 85 per cent of its normal level`
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- (2)(a) Where the occurrence is a discontinuance of business, a permanent restructuring of activity or an act
-- of God, the stoppage terminates "when the level of the work-force or of the activity attains at least 85 per
-- cent of that normal level, with the normal level adjusted by taking that occurrence into account": either
-- level reaching its adjusted 85 per cent is enough (fork F14).
-- (2)(b) Where it is a change in economic or market conditions or in technology, the stoppage terminates when
-- (i) there is a resumption of activity at the premises and (ii) the level of the work-force AND of the activity
-- attain at least 85 per cent of the normal level as adjusted.
-- src:803 | (2) Where, in respect of a stoppage of work, an occurrence prevents the attainment of at least 85 per cent of the normal level of the work-force or activity in respect of the production of goods or services at a factory, workshop or other premises, the stoppage of work terminates
-- src:804 | (a) if the occurrence is a discontinuance of business, a permanent restructuring of activity or an act of God, when the level of the work-force or of the activity attains at least 85 per cent of that normal level, with the normal level adjusted by taking that occurrence into account; and
-- src:805 | (b) if the occurrence is a change in economic or market conditions or in technology, when
-- src:806 | (i) there is a resumption of activity at the factory, workshop or other premises, and
-- src:807 | (ii) the level of the work-force and of the activity attains at least 85 per cent of that normal level as adjusted by taking that occurrence into account.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 53(2) (src:803-807)
GIVEN occurrence IS AN `er3 Occurrence preventing the attainment of the 85 per cent level`
      `there is a resumption of activity at the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work-force is at least 85 per cent of its normal level as adjusted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the level of activity is at least 85 per cent of its normal level as adjusted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 53(2) the stoppage of work is terminated although an occurrence prevents the 85 per cent level` IS
    CONSIDER occurrence
    WHEN `er3 occurrence: a discontinuance of business` THEN `the work-force is at least 85 per cent of its normal level as adjusted` OR `the level of activity is at least 85 per cent of its normal level as adjusted`
    WHEN `er3 occurrence: a permanent restructuring of activity` THEN `the work-force is at least 85 per cent of its normal level as adjusted` OR `the level of activity is at least 85 per cent of its normal level as adjusted`
    WHEN `er3 occurrence: an act of God` THEN `the work-force is at least 85 per cent of its normal level as adjusted` OR `the level of activity is at least 85 per cent of its normal level as adjusted`
    WHEN `er3 occurrence: a change in economic or market conditions` THEN `there is a resumption of activity at the premises` AND `the work-force is at least 85 per cent of its normal level as adjusted` AND `the level of activity is at least 85 per cent of its normal level as adjusted`
    WHEN `er3 occurrence: a change in technology` THEN `there is a resumption of activity at the premises` AND `the work-force is at least 85 per cent of its normal level as adjusted` AND `the level of activity is at least 85 per cent of its normal level as adjusted`
    WHEN `er3 occurrence: none` THEN FALSE
